Chapter 6: Building the Qubit Hamiltonian
==========================================

The complete 15-term H₂ Hamiltonian (Jordan-Wigner):

   1. -0.8122  IIII    [diagonal]
   2. +0.1714  ZIII    [diagonal]
   3. +0.1714  IZII    [diagonal]
   4. -0.2234  IIZI    [diagonal]
   5. -0.2234  IIIZ    [diagonal]
   6. +0.1687  ZZII    [diagonal]
   7. +0.0453  YXXY    [configuration coupling]
   8. -0.0453  YYXX    [configuration coupling]
   9. -0.0453  XXYY    [configuration coupling]
  10. +0.0453  XYYX    [configuration coupling]
  11. +0.1206  ZIZI    [diagonal]
  12. +0.1659  ZIIZ    [diagonal]
  13. +0.1659  IZZI    [diagonal]
  14. +0.1206  IZIZ    [diagonal]
  15. +0.1744  IIZZ    [diagonal]

  Diagonal terms: 11
  Configuration-coupling terms: 4

  Coupling enables determinant mixing; correlation energy is the
  optimized expectation difference of the full Hamiltonian.

